WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:05.766
Gel lifting a little, so you just peel it off? Here's what your natural nail goes through!

2
00:00:05.766 --> 00:00:12.082
The top layer comes off, the nail gets thinner, and here's how gel is removed properly at the salon.

3
00:00:12.082 --> 00:00:15.832
Gel bonds tightly to the top layer of your natural nail.

4
00:00:15.832 --> 00:00:21.248
When you peel it, the gel doesn't come off alone: it takes a thin layer of nail with it.

5
00:00:21.248 --> 00:00:27.305
After peeling, the surface is rough with white patches, and the nail is thin and soft.

6
00:00:27.305 --> 00:00:31.878
It breaks and splits easily, and it can even feel tender to the touch.

7
00:00:31.878 --> 00:00:38.217
The right way: at the salon, the colour is filed down and the gel is softened with remover.

8
00:00:38.217 --> 00:00:43.485
The softened gel is lifted off gently, and your natural nail stays intact.

9
00:00:43.485 --> 00:00:48.539
If you've already peeled it, cut your nails short and apply cuticle oil every day.

10
00:00:48.539 --> 00:00:52.193
Your nails will get stronger as the new nail grows out.

11
00:00:52.193 --> 00:01:00.118
In short: gel holds tightly, peeling leaves the nail thinner, so have it removed at the salon and care for your nails with oil.

12
00:01:00.118 --> 00:01:05.151
Gel lifting? Book a refill at Moja Beauty, and we'll remove it the right way!

13
00:01:05.151 --> 00:01:11.424
